# Line-ending policy
# =================
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites line endings on checkout. That is harmless for source, but it makes
# a byte-for-byte hash of a text file irreproducible: the bytes on disk depend
# on the checkout, not on what was committed.
#
# Two file classes here are hashed or fed to E3D verbatim, so their bytes must
# survive a round trip unchanged.

# Verbatim user evidence. These files record what the user observed in a real
# E3D session and are the basis of every VERIFIED claim in skill/knowledge/.
# tests/test_extrusion_study.py asserts their SHA-256. Never normalised, never
# translated, never reformatted -- see SKILL.md, "Writing language".
Projects/**/results/evidence/** -text

# Generated macros and native E3D exports. E3D's macro reader is sensitive to
# stray CR characters, and wsb/pml_compare.py diffs exports line by line.
*.pml -text
*.mac -text

# Binary project data, listed explicitly so Git never attempts a text merge.
*.xlsx binary
*.dwg  binary
*.png  binary
